)^{p+1})\\,\\text{as}\\,Δx\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThe order describes how fast errors shrink as $Δx$ decreases.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option in turn:\n\n- For $τ(Δx)=2(Δx)^{6}+5(Δx)^{7},$ the dominant term as $Δx\\to 0$ is $2(Δx)^{6}=2(Δx)^{5+1}.$\nSo, statement I corresponds to an order $5$ method.\n\n- For $τ(Δx)=0.4(Δx)^{4}+8(Δx)^{9},$ the dominant term as $Δx\\to 0$ is $0.4(Δx)^{4}=0.4(Δx)^{3+1}.$\nSo, statement II corresponds to an order $3$ method.\n\n- For $τ(Δx)=6(Δx)^{5}+3(Δx)^{8},$ the dominant term as $Δx\\to 0$ is $6(Δx)^{5}=6(Δx)^{4+1}.$\nSo, statement III corresponds to an order $4$ method.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139535029 true] [17592186327746 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327747 13194139535029 true] [17592186327746 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327748 13194139535029 true] [17592186327746 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327749 13194139535029 true] [17592186327746 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327750 13194139535029 true] [17592186327746 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327751 13194139535029 true] [17592186327746 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535029 true] [17592186327746 1041 "selection" 13194139535029 true] [17592186327746 1104 #edb/ref 17592186327749 13194139535029 true] [17592186327746 1110 #uuid "ba6975a0-81ff-5083-b52b-d9573759633c" 13194139535029 true] [17592186327747 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535029 true] [17592186327747 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535029 true] [17592186327747 1111 #uuid "b9dfb73f-753f-517e-a9fb-21d03f7bdb68" 13194139535029 true] [17592186327748 1034 "I only" 13194139535029 true] [17592186327748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535029 true] [17592186327748 1111 #uuid "a2ab14e2-4a0d-5806-be60-34f002513326" 13194139535029 true] [17592186327749 1034 "III only" 13194139535029 true] [17592186327749 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535029 true] [17592186327749 1111 #uuid "2d7b88ea-814f-5b4a-81c1-4c220ead7a1b" 13194139535029 true] [17592186327750 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535029 true] [17592186327750 1103 #edb